                        ],
                        "form": "шараба́не"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1b2e7dda-a9d6-4bac-a9b3-ea62111573c7",
                        "entry_id": "a16b4012-7767-3a6b-87b2-5115bc5546be",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "шараба́нах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7e7f8b6e-ac3a-3e67-9951-901f31896fb9",
                        "entry_id": "a16b4012-7767-3a6b-87b2-5115bc5546be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. тип открытой повозки для прогулок, загородных поездок, охоты, изначально были запряжены лошадьми, позже появились моторные"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "476901c7-cbb9-431c-ba63-2e2eda8f3ca6",
                                "sense_id": "7e7f8b6e-ac3a-3e67-9951-901f31896fb9",
                                "text": "Гаганов с Маврикием Николаевичем прибыли на место в щёгольском шарабане парой, которым правил Артемий Павлович; при них находился слуга."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0ea2000-d1de-4395-89cd-f87e6a164fdf",
                                "sense_id": "7e7f8b6e-ac3a-3e67-9951-901f31896fb9",
                                "text": "Перед глазами всё носится, в ушах всё шумит Париж ― лунные фонари его даже мерещатся в зрачках, как бельма, и катится он передо мной в омнибусах, шарабанах, каретах etc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79a52b72-618e-4b2a-bda4-b04f7cd9762e",
                                "sense_id": "7e7f8b6e-ac3a-3e67-9951-901f31896fb9",
                                "text": "Он спросил, как поживает его чудак-приятель с молодою женой, и, осмотрев беглым взглядом непаристых лошадей и с заплатанными крыльями коляску, предложил дамам ехать в шарабане."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "751e6c97-49b8-312f-bbba-68d24052908c",
                        "entry_id": "a16b4012-7767-3a6b-87b2-5115bc5546be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "рег. зимний рыбацкий ящик для снастей и улова"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88411e0c-48af-44d3-98c6-da066a5461c7",
                                "sense_id": "751e6c97-49b8-312f-bbba-68d24052908c",
                                "text": "Наловили целый шарабан окуней."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3186015-12a2-3b61-bd1a-7fa80f92ae8f",
                        "entry_id": "a16b4012-7767-3a6b-87b2-5115bc5546be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "рег. приспособление для горячего копчения"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a09ca7bf-7e88-4fcf-956c-eae7772218dc",
                                "sense_id": "a3186015-12a2-3b61-bd1a-7fa80f92ae8f",
                                "text": "Сегодня угощали шарабаном, в нем был толстолоб и ленок (рыба) с начинкой из капусты. Шарабан — это гриль, горячее копчение."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "18f1b65a-301d-432c-96bc-590c199ac61e",
                        "source_entry_id": "a16b4012-7767-3a6b-87b2-5115bc5546be",
                        "target_lang_word": "charabanc",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "charabanc",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "578a96f9-e066-356e-95ee-2276f0d10a1a",
                                        "entry_id": "ecb65926-21a6-363f-b48b-1f903f478cd9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A horse-drawn, and then later, motorized omnibus with open sides, and often, no roof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e33841da-b605-44b6-9e7b-20b615d9a723",
                                                "sense_id": "578a96f9-e066-356e-95ee-2276f0d10a1a",
                                                "text": "A little further on, to the right, was a large garage, where the charabancs stood, half in and half out of the yard."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2118e592-e09b-4016-b0e6-cb19ff95e515",
                                                "sense_id": "578a96f9-e066-356e-95ee-2276f0d10a1a",
                                                "text": "And full of colored dreams / Deep inside a rainbow / Lived Happiness Stan / In a small Victorian charabanc"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb89f55e-4298-4340-854e-cf481d09546d",
                                                "sense_id": "578a96f9-e066-356e-95ee-2276f0d10a1a",
                                                "text": "The cumbersome though finely painted charabanc of the late James style is pulled swaying along by a frisky pony of a plot farcical and romantic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7331fd7e-1daf-3408-8c73-534e850253fb",
                                        "entry_id": "ecb65926-21a6-363f-b48b-1f903f478cd9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bus, especially one hired by groups for pleasure outings, what was later called a coach."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "573cb7fe-5b42-4f4e-a792-6aca3569fb60",
                                                "sense_id": "7331fd7e-1daf-3408-8c73-534e850253fb",
                                                "text": "Oh shit, there goes the charabanc!\nLooks like I'm gonna be stuck here the whole summer"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eeee2549-2806-4933-8a0b-d9ca9f4e92a1",
                                                "sense_id": "7331fd7e-1daf-3408-8c73-534e850253fb",
                                                "text": "Mum had worked there as a teenager and once recalled her duty of having to meet the charabancs that brought the well-heeled to the baths from Droitwich station before the war."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "520e3cbc-c5f6-3ed6-938a-e54793c01304",
                                        "entry_id": "ecb65926-21a6-363f-b48b-1f903f478cd9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vehicle that is slow, overcrowded, or otherwise undesirable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3181a0d5-daa1-4811-96af-1395004e40b3",
                                                "sense_id": "520e3cbc-c5f6-3ed6-938a-e54793c01304",
                                                "text": "We return to the charabanc of a car to find a swarm of children dancing round it, clambering up the back, jumping on the step; the driver sleeps peacefully at the wheel, oblivious of their shrieks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b4288aa-4ec7-4da3-b03b-9ab87cdd2f62",
                                                "sense_id": "520e3cbc-c5f6-3ed6-938a-e54793c01304",
                                                "text": "Just as I'm thinking my plan has failed an old charabanc of a vehicle slows down and starts hooting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13721b50-b9c6-41ed-a148-58892268244a",
                                                "sense_id": "520e3cbc-c5f6-3ed6-938a-e54793c01304",
                                                "text": "It was lucky therefore that I kept an eye on the quayside blackboard by the stern of the \"Patmos Star\", a charabanc of a daytrip boat that was to transport me and my bags to the tiny island of Lipsí, a short hop from Patmos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e90e1cb-f578-4268-a7ba-c1af94545110",
                                                "sense_id": "520e3cbc-c5f6-3ed6-938a-e54793c01304",
                                                "text": "[…] but Mark has never even sat on a motorbike, let alone ridden one before and certainly not with a rowboat attached and a spasmatic dog riding pillion. It was nice to see that there was stillsome good old-fashioned British embarrassment left, as straggling past Philippe with a muttered \"Au revoir, Breton.\", we pushed the whole charabanc a mile up the road until there was no sign of habitation; in France even the lamp-posts have eyes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d5ae2c0-5406-494b-bee2-def7053003df",
                                                "sense_id": "520e3cbc-c5f6-3ed6-938a-e54793c01304",
                                                "text": "The lantern got closer until eventually the sound, smell and heat of dogs was upon them, and a train of huskies stopped in a great cloud of steam. The whole charabanc emitted a strong smell of hot stew, which my mum remembers as the most heavenly thing she had ever smelt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5293efd-6d04-3e77-bb69-e70e120a4a6a",
                                        "entry_id": "ecb65926-21a6-363f-b48b-1f903f478cd9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An elaborate production or endeavor involving many people or things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5207ee8-621a-4c5d-ae19-c9da7d070eb2",
                                                "sense_id": "a5293efd-6d04-3e77-bb69-e70e120a4a6a",
                                                "text": "For all their lean and hungry look, and for all they wear the simplest of dhotis around their loins, they usually have clever accomplices in the crowd, and a whole charabanc full of invisible wires and concealed cabinets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86b2ac4d-7a71-41da-8582-83729caa65b0",
                                                "sense_id": "a5293efd-6d04-3e77-bb69-e70e120a4a6a",
                                                "text": "He comes along all dressed up in the real deal costume, all the sequins and rhinestone, the heavyweight boxing belt, the cape, the whole charabanc, you know?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed5c30e2-d283-44fa-9000-6721233f3124",
                                                "sense_id": "a5293efd-6d04-3e77-bb69-e70e120a4a6a",
                                                "text": "Schuman's European Coal and Steel Community in 1951, which set the whole charabanc rolling, operated in the interests of producers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8170a6ef-a88e-4ac0-a728-56c615e2ba3c",
                                                "sense_id": "a5293efd-6d04-3e77-bb69-e70e120a4a6a",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, I felt responsible. I'd started the whole charabanc. It was my band."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "charabanc",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
